                <pb facs="0563" n="545" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v12p1/pg545"/>


                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Proposed Agreed Minute</hi></head>
                <p>If Communist China should commit overt, unprovoked military aggression in the
                    Western Pacific or Southeast Asia, the government of each member state would at
                    once: <list>
                        <label>a.</label>
                        <item>request approval from its Congress or Parliament for the use of its
                            armed forces against Communist China to defeat the aggression;</item>
                        <label>b.</label>
                        <item>support an appeal to the United Nations by the parties attacked for
                            assistance against the aggression; and,</item>
                        <label>c.</label>
                        <item>seek to persuade other free nations to join in the action with such
                            help as each can give.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
